# `protocol::OpBinary::encode_op`/`decode_op` (../🦀️.rs) forward straight to
# `dsl::variants_binary::encode_op`/`decode_op` — this was ALREADY real binary before this
# program touched it, NOT the F6-era `print_op().into_bytes()` text-as-binary shortcut
# (confirmed by direct reading: `encode_op` calls `os_pack::encode_record_body`, never
# `print_op`). Layout, byte-for-byte, per that helper's own doc comment (`OP_BINARY_FORMAT`):
# a fixed `format` byte (always `1`), the matched variant's ordinal as a `varint`
# (declaration order, `NoMutation` dropped: `SetSnapshot`=0, `SetScreenSize`=1,
# `SetGlobalColorTable`=2, `SetBackgroundColorIndex`=3, `SetPixelAspectRatio`=4,
# `SetLoopCount`=5, `InsertFrame`=6, `RemoveFrame`=7, `MoveFrame`=8, `SetFrameGeometry`=9,
# `SetFramePixels`=10, `SetFrameInterlace`=11, `SetFrameDelay`=12, `SetFrameDisposal`=13,
# `SetFrameTransparency`=14, `SetFrameUserInput`=15, `InsertComment`=16, `RemoveComment`=17,
# `AddAppExtension`=18, `RemoveAppExtension`=19 — `dsl::DslVariants::variants()`'s own
# emission order), then the variant's own field payload,
# `os_pack::encode_record_body(spec, record)` — itself a varint-prefixed STRING-SYMBOL TABLE
# followed by a generic, self-describing per-field-id TAG+value wire. This inner wire is the
# FRAMEWORK's own generic record-body encoding — shared verbatim by every
# `#[derive(dsl::DslRecord)]`/`DslOps`/`DslDiff` type in the whole repo, not anything specific
# to `stdio.gif.89a`, and is genuinely NOT expressible by this dialect's `Array`/`Ref`/
# `repeat` primitives as they stand today (no dynamic per-field TAG dispatch keyed by a
# runtime field-id, no symbol-table back-reference resolution) — the same
# `txt-opbinary-record-body-wire-is-framework-generic` gap txt's own sibling protocol file
# documents (`📄️txt/…/🧬️mutations/💾️binary/📡️.protocol.semio`) and 87a's own sibling
# protocol file, copied verbatim per its own "copy the shape" instruction. Modeled honestly:
# `format`/`ordinal` are genuinely, individually byte-walked and validated; the remaining
# record-body bytes are one opaque tail.
framing record
field format u8
field ordinal varint
chain bytes
